WEBVTT

00:00:00.051 --> 00:00:02.228
Two handkerchiefs and a pink ribbon:

00:00:02.238 --> 00:00:04.308
that's how this bra patent began.

00:00:04.318 --> 00:00:05.096
New York.

00:00:05.106 --> 00:00:07.071
Young Mary Phelps Jacob is dressing for

00:00:07.081 --> 00:00:07.809
a ball.

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:09.718
Her corset's whalebones
poke out through the

00:00:09.728 --> 00:00:10.711
sheer gown.

00:00:10.721 --> 00:00:12.661
So, with her maid, she stitches something

00:00:12.671 --> 00:00:13.375
better.

00:00:13.385 --> 00:00:16.548
In 1914 she files this:

00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:22.524
US patent 1,115,674, a backless brassiere.

00:00:22.624 --> 00:00:25.909
A corset maker,
Warner Brothers, bought her

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:27.293
patent for $1,500.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:28.895
But she didn't invent the first bra

00:00:28.905 --> 00:00:29.556
ever.

00:00:29.566 --> 00:00:31.893
In 2008, at a castle in Austria,

00:00:31.903 --> 00:00:35.790
archaeologists found four
linen bras with cups,

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:37.119
from the 1400s.

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:38.917
So the bra is at least 500

00:00:38.927 --> 00:00:40.579
years older than her patent.

00:00:40.589 --> 00:00:42.114
And hers began with...
